Alembic migrations for the Neighborhood Issue Reporter backend.

Run every command from the `backend/` directory, with the virtual environment
active and DATABASE_URL set in `.env`.

    alembic current                 show the applied revision
    alembic history --verbose       list all revisions
    alembic upgrade head            apply everything
    alembic downgrade -1            undo the last revision
    alembic upgrade head --sql      print SQL without connecting

The revision chain starts at `0001_core` (users + departments). The
report-domain migration must use `down_revision = "0001_core"` so the two
developers' schemas apply in a defined order.

The database URL is read from the application settings in `env.py`, not from
`alembic.ini`. Never put credentials in a committed file.
